# Project R library
#
# This file is an example. Do not commit a machine-specific absolute path.
# The package library is the directory `.Rlib` next to this repository
# (the parent folder of the repo), not a folder inside the repo.
#
# From the repository root, in the shell:
#
#   export R_LIBS_USER="$(CDPATH= cd -- .. && pwd)/.Rlib"
#   mkdir -p "$R_LIBS_USER"
#
# R 4.2.2 matches Bioconductor 3.16. Install into that library only:
#
#   CRAN: vegan igraph ggraph circlize ggrepel patchwork ggtext
#   Bioconductor 3.16 (BiocManager): ComplexHeatmap ggtree
#
# Copy what you need into an untracked `.Renviron` if you want R to see the
# library without exporting the variable. Leave the expanded path out of git.
